{"en":[{"partOfSpeech":"Adverb","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt50\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> In a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/good\" title=\"good\">good</a> way; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/accurately\" title=\"accurately\">accurately</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/competently\" title=\"competently\">competently</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/satisfactorily\" title=\"satisfactorily\">satisfactorily</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"He does his job <b>well</b>."},{"example":"My <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/RV#English\" title=\"RV\">RV</a> runs <b>well</b> on diesel."},{"example":"The jacket looks good and fits you <b>well</b>."},{"example":"Recent events do not augur <b>well</b> for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/world_peace#English\" title=\"world peace\">world peace</a>."}],"examples":["He does his job <b>well</b>.","My <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/RV#English\" title=\"RV\">RV</a> runs <b>well</b> on diesel.","The jacket looks good and fits you <b>well</b>.","Recent events do not augur <b>well</b> for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/world_peace#English\" title=\"world peace\">world peace</a>."]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt58\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/completely\" title=\"completely\">Completely</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/fully\" title=\"fully\">fully</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"I prefer a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/well_done#English\" title=\"well done\"><b>well</b> done</a> steak."},{"example":"Cook the potatoes <b>well</b> to ensure they aren't tough."},{"example":"We’re <b>well</b> beat now."},{"example":"I was <b>well</b> looked after by close relations."}],"examples":["I prefer a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/well_done#English\" title=\"well done\"><b>well</b> done</a> steak.","Cook the potatoes <b>well</b> to ensure they aren't tough.","We’re <b>well</b> beat now.","I was <b>well</b> looked after by close relations."]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt65\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> To a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/significant\" title=\"significant\">significant</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/degree\" title=\"degree\">degree</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"That author is <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/well_known#English\" title=\"well known\"><b>well</b> known</a>."},{"example":"A monument <b>well</b> worth seeing"}],"examples":["That author is <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/well_known#English\" title=\"well known\"><b>well</b> known</a>.","A monument <b>well</b> worth seeing"]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt71\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/very\" title=\"very\">Very</a> (as a general-purpose intensifier)."},{"definition":"In a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/desirable\" title=\"desirable\">desirable</a> manner; so as one could wish; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/satisfactorily\" title=\"satisfactorily\">satisfactorily</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/favourably\" title=\"favourably\">favourably</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/advantageously\" title=\"advantageously\">advantageously</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"I'm glad Joe got fired last week. I think we're <b>well</b> rid of him."}],"examples":["I'm glad Joe got fired last week. I think we're <b>well</b> rid of him."]}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Adjective","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"In good <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/health\" title=\"health\">health</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"I've been sick, but now I'm <b>well</b>."},{"example":"I've always been a healthy, fit woman, but right now I really don't feel very <b>well</b>."}],"examples":["I've been sick, but now I'm <b>well</b>.","I've always been a healthy, fit woman, but right now I really don't feel very <b>well</b>."]},{"definition":"Highly satisfactory","parsedExamples":[{"example":"Everything <b>well</b> with you<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span>"}],"examples":["Everything <b>well</b> with you<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span>"]},{"definition":"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/good\" title=\"good\">Good</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/content\" title=\"content\">content</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"“How are you<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span>” — “I'm <b>well</b>, thank you<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">!</span>”"}],"examples":["“How are you<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span>” — “I'm <b>well</b>, thank you<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">!</span>”"]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt110\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/prudent\" title=\"prudent\">Prudent</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/good\" title=\"good\">good</a>; well-<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/advised\" title=\"advised\">advised</a>."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt114\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> Good to eat; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/tasty\" title=\"tasty\">tasty</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/delicious\" title=\"delicious\">delicious</a>."}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Interjection","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt129\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">Used as a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/discourse_marker#English\" title=\"discourse marker\">discourse marker</a>.</span>","parsedExamples":[{"example":"“So, what have you been doing<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span>” “<b>Well</b>, we went for a picnic<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">;</span> and then it started raining, so we came home early.”"},{"example":"“The car is broken.” “<b>Well</b>, we could walk to the movies instead.”"},{"example":"“I didn't like the music.” “<b>Well</b>, I thought it was good.”"},{"example":"I forgot to pack the tent<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">!</span> <b>Well</b>, I guess we’re sleeping under the stars tonight."},{"example":"It was a bit... <b>well</b>, too loud."}],"examples":["“So, what have you been doing<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span>” “<b>Well</b>, we went for a picnic<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">;</span> and then it started raining, so we came home early.”","“The car is broken.” “<b>Well</b>, we could walk to the movies instead.”","“I didn't like the music.” “<b>Well</b>, I thought it was good.”","I forgot to pack the tent<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">!</span> <b>Well</b>, I guess we’re sleeping under the stars tonight.","It was a bit... <b>well</b>, too loud."]},{"definition":"<span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt132\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">Used as a <span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/hedge#English:_Q474726\" title=\"hedge\">hedge</a></span>.</span>","parsedExamples":[{"example":"“The car is broken.” “<b>Well</b>, we could walk to the movies instead.”"},{"example":"“I didn't like the music.” “<b>Well</b>, I thought it was good.”"},{"example":"I forgot to pack the tent<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">!</span> <b>Well</b>, I guess we’re sleeping under the stars tonight."}],"examples":["“The car is broken.” “<b>Well</b>, we could walk to the movies instead.”","“I didn't like the music.” “<b>Well</b>, I thought it was good.”","I forgot to pack the tent<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">!</span> <b>Well</b>, I guess we’re sleeping under the stars tonight."]},{"definition":"<span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt138\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">Expressing reluctance to say something.</span>","parsedExamples":[{"example":"It was a bit... <b>well</b>, too loud."}],"examples":["It was a bit... <b>well</b>, too loud."]},{"definition":"<span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt141\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">An exclamation of sarcastic surprise (often doubled or tripled and in a lowering intonation).</span>","parsedExamples":[{"example":"<b>Well</b>, <b>well</b>, <b>well</b>, what do we have here<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span>"}],"examples":["<b>Well</b>, <b>well</b>, <b>well</b>, what do we have here<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span>"]},{"definition":"<span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt143\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">An exclamation of indignance.</span>","parsedExamples":[{"example":"<b>Well</b><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">!</span> There was no need to say that in front of my mother<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">!</span>"}],"examples":["<b>Well</b><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">!</span> There was no need to say that in front of my mother<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">!</span>"]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt145\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt146\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">Used as a greeting</span>, short for \"Are you well?\"","parsedExamples":[{"example":"<b>Well</b>, lads<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span> How's things<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span>"}],"examples":["<b>Well</b>, lads<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span> How's things<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span>"]},{"definition":"<span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt148\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">Used as a question to demand an answer from someone.</span>","parsedExamples":[{"example":"And what do you think you're doing<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span> ... <b>Well<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span></b>"}],"examples":["And what do you think you're doing<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span> ... <b>Well<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">?</span></b>"]}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":""},{"definition":"A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/hole\" title=\"hole\">hole</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/sunk\" title=\"sunk\">sunk</a> into the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/ground\" title=\"ground\">ground</a> as a source of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/water\" title=\"water\">water</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/oil\" title=\"oil\">oil</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/natural_gas\" title=\"natural gas\">natural gas</a> or other fluids."},{"definition":"A place where a liquid such as water surfaces naturally; a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/spring\" title=\"spring\">spring</a>."},{"definition":"A small <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/depression\" title=\"depression\">depression</a>, e.g. suitable for holding <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/liquid\" title=\"liquid\">liquid</a> or other objects.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"Make a <b>well</b> in the dough mixture and pour in the milk."}],"examples":["Make a <b>well</b> in the dough mixture and pour in the milk."]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt202\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> A source of supply."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt206\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> A vertical, cylindrical <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/trunk\" title=\"trunk\">trunk</a> in a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/ship\" title=\"ship\">ship</a>, reaching down to the lowest part of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/hull\" title=\"hull\">hull</a>, through which the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/bilge_pump\" title=\"bilge pump\">bilge pumps</a> operate."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt207\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/cockpit\" title=\"cockpit\">cockpit</a> of a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/sailboat\" title=\"sailboat\">sailboat</a>."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt208\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> A compartment in the middle of the hold of a fishing vessel, made tight at the sides, but having holes perforated in the bottom to let in water to keep fish alive while they are transported to market."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt209\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> A vertical passage in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/stern\" title=\"stern\">stern</a> into which an <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/auxiliary\" title=\"auxiliary\">auxiliary</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/screw\" title=\"screw\">screw</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/propeller\" title=\"propeller\">propeller</a> may be drawn up out of the water."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt210\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> A hole or excavation in the earth, in mining, from which run branches or galleries."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt211\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> An opening through the floors of a building, as for a staircase or an elevator; a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/wellhole\" title=\"wellhole\">wellhole</a>."},{"definition":"The open space between the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/bench\" title=\"bench\">bench</a> and the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/counsel\" title=\"counsel\">counsel</a> tables in a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/courtroom\" title=\"courtroom\">courtroom</a>."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt212\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> The lower part of a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/furnace\" title=\"furnace\">furnace</a>, into which the metal falls."},{"definition":"A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/well_drink\" title=\"well drink\">well drink</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"They're having a special tonight<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">:</span> $1 <b>wells</b>."}],"examples":["They're having a special tonight<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">:</span> $1 <b>wells</b>."]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt214\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/playfield\" title=\"playfield\">playfield</a> of <i><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Tetris\" title=\"Tetris\">Tetris</a></i> and similar video games, into which the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/block\" title=\"block\">blocks</a> fall."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt216\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> In a microtiter plate, each of the small equal circular or square sections which serve as test tubes."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt217\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> The region of an <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/interface\" title=\"interface\">interface</a> that contains <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/tab\" title=\"tab\">tabs</a>."}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Verb","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt251\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> To issue forth, as water from the earth; to flow; to spring."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt254\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> To have something seep out of the surface.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"Her eyes <b>welled</b> with tears."}],"examples":["Her eyes <b>welled</b> with tears."]}]}],"de":[{"partOfSpeech":"Verb","language":"German","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"form-of-definition use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt269\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#singular_number\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">singular</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#imperative_mood\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">imperative</a> of <span class=\"form-of-definition-link\"><i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"de\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/wellen#German\" title=\"wellen\">wellen</a></i></span></span>"},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt270\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <span class=\"form-of-definition use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt271\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#first_person\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">first-person</a> <a rel=\"mw:Wiki